      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While soap and peroxide can clean minor scrapes, they are not recommended for deep puncture wounds because they can introduce bacteria and delay the natural healing process. Rusty metal from a trowel carries a significant risk of infection, so it is much safer to take you to a doctor or urgent care where they can thoroughly clean the wound, provide a tetanus shot if necessary, and start antibiotics to prevent complications. Trying to manage a deep rusty puncture wound at home could lead to serious fever or infection issues that require medical treatment.",
